The Administration shall be responsible for the following matters:
1.planning, promotion and implementation of policies, as well as the drafting of laws and regulations regarding child and youth welfare and rights, and family welfare services;
2.planning, promotion and implementation of policies, as well as the drafting of laws and regulations regarding child and youth protection, out-of-home care, support for independent living, and care;
3.planning, promotion and implementation of resources, as well as the drafting of laws and regulations regarding child, youth and family support services;
4.planning, promotion and implementation of policies, as well as the drafting of laws and regulations regarding reproductive and childcare service resources;
5.promotion, coordination and liaison regarding the Convention on the Rights of the Child, as well as the supervision and execution of impact assessments;
6.promotion and coordination of policies regarding child and youth recreation, play, and leisure;
7.cross-agency policy coordination and integration regarding counseling for child and youth deviant behaviors;
8.planning, promotion and implementation of policies, as well as the drafting of laws and regulations regarding development and advancement of child and youth rights, and their participation in public affairs;
9.planning, promotion, implementation and coordination of policies regarding vital statistics, physical and mental health promotion, preventive healthcare, accident and injury prevention, and medical care for children and youth;
10.planning, promotion and implementation of early intervention;
11.supervision, counseling and evaluation of the operations of child and youth welfare institutions;
12.development of Information and Communications Technology (ICT) applications, international cooperation, and engagement regarding child, youth and family support services;
13.cross-agency policy coordination, integration, supervision, counseling and evaluation of matters concerning child, youth and family support welfare services;
14.planning, implementation and cross-agency policy coordination regarding child and youth cyber safety and protection of personal data rights; and
15.other matters related to child and youth welfare and rights, health promotion, and family support welfare services.
